OL,3,AMeta continues to run ads promoting
OL,4,Achild sexual abuse material in India -
OL,5,Areport
OL,6,
OL,7,FWarning: This story contains
OL,8,Fdescriptions of abuse
OL,10,FMeta ran hundreds of paid ads with
OL,11,Fartificial intelligence-generated child
OL,12,Fsexual abuse imagery, including several
OL,13,Fin India, over the past 10 months, a
OL,14,Fnew report by US-based campaigners has
OL,15,Ffound.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,107,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11904
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1788945549
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AMeta continues to run ads promoting
OL,4,Achild sexual abuse material in India -
OL,5,Areport
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe report comes two months after the
OL,8,FIndian government ordered Meta to
OL,9,Fremove all ads and content promoting
OL,10,Fchild sexual abuse material (CSAM) on
OL,11,FInstagram. This was in the aftermath of
OL,12,Fa BBC Eye investigation which found
OL,13,Fthat Instagram was running paid adverts
OL,14,Fpromoting CSAM in India.
OL,16,FWashington-based Tech Transparency
OL,17,FProject (TTP) says it found 332 adverts
OL,18,Fwith CSAM that ran on Facebook and
OL,19,FInstagram, the majority of them (274)
OL,20,Fin August this year.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG4/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,107,105,200,160,0,100
